text.section:
A licensee shall file a written report with the Commissioner within 15 days of becoming aware of the occurrence of any of the following:

The filing for bankruptcy or reorganization by the licensee;


The institution of revocation or suspension proceedings against the licensee by any state or governmental authority;


The denial of the opportunity of the licensee to engage in business by any state or governmental authority;


Any felony indictment of the licensee or any of its employees, officers, directors, or principals;


Any felony conviction of the licensee or any of its employees, officers, directors, or principals; and


Such other events as the Commissioner may determine and identify by regulation.
